// An unresolved NAME inside an uninstantiated generic body. Name resolution was deferred to instantiation
// along with everything else, so a typo'd call in a template nobody used never surfaced at all.
// The call mentions no type parameter, so the probe walk resolves it exactly as any other call.
fn void neverCalled<T>(T unused) {
    undefinedFunction(a: 1);     // ERROR: no such function
}
fn int32 main() { return 0; }
